  <notes>
    <note date="2026-10-07">FOLLOW-UP FIX: word-add-in-r1 created a separate PRODUCTION add-in app, "Spaarke Office Add-in (Production)" 1958aec2-0218-495e-8e3c-37133e9b8357 (master cbee69b68); c1258e2d is the dev identity, which calls only the dev BFF. The Worker Bicep default preAuthorizedClientAppIds is now 1958aec2 (customer stamps are production); platform-controlplane.json rebuilt; guide H3 + §7.3 and the inventory corrected. 1958aec2 is single-tenant too, so the multi-tenant recommendation (coordination -4 addendum) covers both apps.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-07">COMPLETED. Commits b0e244c17 (steps 1-4) + the review-fix commit. ControlPlane 2307/0 (1 skip), ArchTests 841/841, Api/Worker 0 warnings, catalog generator -Verify OK, platform-controlplane.json rebuilt in sync.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-07">LIVE ACTIONS (owner-approved, outside the code): Static Web Apps swa-spaarke-office-addins-prod and swa-spaarke-external-spa-prod in rg-spaarke-shared-prod; custom domains addins.spaarke.com and external.spaarke.com (owner added the Namecheap CNAMEs); both Ready with managed certificates. Recorded in notes/t240-plan.md.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-07">DEVIATIONS (directional steps; acceptance criteria amended here): (a) AC1 — no Dataverse origin or `.api.` variant in Cors__AllowedOrigins: CorsModule already admits *.dynamics.com / *.powerapps.com by suffix, so those entries would change nothing; the list carries the two shared client sites as manifest literals, which keeps it non-empty (the startup failure). (b) Constraint "shared origins per platform environment" — one global literal list: every stamp is reached by the same production client sites (K4: dev/staging stamps get the production origins; no failure today). (c) AC3 — origins are build-time literals, so the refusal is a build-time test (FilePerEnvSettingsManifestTests: exact https origins) plus CorsModule's own startup check, not a run-time H4b failure. (d) Step 3 — no H13 probe for a shared origin: H4b's and H13's /healthz already prove the BFF started with a valid list, and the values are pinned by the manifest test.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-07">FOUND + FIXED IN SCOPE: (1) F1 — the Worker never set EntraAppRegOptions__SpaarkeTenantId, so every Model 1 run (profile spaarke-hosted-model2) failed at H3's FIC step; the Worker Bicep sets it from tenant().tenantId. (2) F1 (review, tenant isolation, pre-existing) — H3 adopted ANY registration named spaarke-bff-api-{customerId}; now refused unless exactly one match, no secret/certificate, no foreign FIC, no owner but the control plane (AdoptionRefusal + appreg-adoption-refused). Live read: the legacy spaarke-bff-api-prod (no owners, 1 client secret) would now be refused for a customer id 'prod'. (3) F2 — config-key names in diagnostics (EntraAppReg: -> EntraAppRegOptions:), stale option docs, dead shell-out options, comments citing a deleted file, swapped test comments; null request lists now mean "leave untouched"; Guid.Empty refused; preAuthorizedClientAppIds threaded through platform-controlplane.bicep.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-07">KNOWN LIMITS / FILED: ISS-003 (#1376) — one registration per customer: a second environment would overwrite the first's redirect/FIC (D6 keeps one environment per customer; binding note in provisioning.md). ISS-004 (#1377) — any Spaarke-tenant user can get any customer BFF token; data access still bounded by the stamp; consider appRoleAssignmentRequired. K2 — a stale read right after the reconcile PATCH fails resumable (appreg-client-access-failed). K3 — runs that completed H3 before this change are not re-applied (none could, SpaarkeTenantId was missing). The acct optional claim on the registration stays with T255.</note>
  </notes>
